        "theme":  "Agents",
        "summary":  "Postman built Agent Mode, an AI-native API testing and documentation interface, on Amazon Bedrock to serve 40 million developers globally, and shares the production architecture patterns behind it. Key design decisions include dynamically narrowing visible tool sets from 170+ to roughly 15 per task, building purpose-built context handlers rather than serializing existing data models, and using tiered prompt caching with geographic inference routing for enterprise data residency compliance. The article reveals that agent effectiveness degrades measurably when tool catalogs exceed approximately 40 tools.",
