        "execSummary":  "The Nemotron-LangChain result challenges the assumption that closed proprietary models are required for top-tier agentic performance, with benchmark-leading accuracy achieved at a fraction of the cost using an open stack. For enterprise leaders evaluating agentic platforms, the 10x inference cost differential is decision-relevant: it shifts the total cost of ownership calculus significantly in favor of open model deployments for high-throughput workflows. The NemoClaw blueprint also addresses the governance concern that open deployments require more internal engineering—NVIDIA provides a complete, tested reference architecture. The watch item is that benchmark performance on agent harnesses does not always translate directly to domain-specific task accuracy, so proof-of-concept testing on real enterprise workloads remains essential before committing to an open-stack strategy.",
