        "execSummary":  "As AI compresses strategy and execution cycles, the leadership behaviors that served CIOs in stable environments are no longer sufficient, and this article offers a peer-sourced model for what replaces them. The seven Cs—from Coherence (linking strategy to execution) to Courage (acting despite incomplete data)—are validated by CIOs at scale enterprises including BNY, J\u0026J, and GSK. The direct implication for senior leaders: organizations that build these capabilities organizationally, not just individually, will out-execute peers in AI adoption speed. The key caveat is that the framework is qualitative and experience-based, not empirically tested, so leaders should treat it as a diagnostic lens rather than a prescriptive roadmap.",
